# Everything here would otherwise be uploaded to the Docker daemon on every
# build. The four big ones are node_modules (104 MB), backend/models (208 MB),
# notebooks (100 MB) and the source artwork for the guides (17 MB).

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`.
node_modules

# Built inside the image by the web stage; a stale local copy must not win.
dist
dist-ssr
.vite

# Weights, the handbook index and the two self-downloading models. Mounted as
# a volume at runtime instead of baked in, so the image stays small and a new
# model does not mean a rebuild.
backend/models

# Training only. Never imported by the server.
notebooks
saans_data

# Source artwork for the question guides, both languages. The built WebP files
# in src/assets/guides/ are what the app uses and those are kept.
src/assets/*.png
src/assets/urdu assstes/

# Secrets. Passed in by compose as environment variables instead.
.env
kaggle.json

.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
*.md
!README.md
